I'm going to commit to the wild swing on **D34 — De Branges Hilbert space `H(E_ξ)` for the Riemann xi-function**. Cross-domain technique never used in the project (de Branges Hilbert spaces of entire functions); the question — "does the projection error of `χ_{[0,x]}` onto the first-N reproducing kernels decay at polylog rate?" — has a concrete, decidable computational test, never published. If it works, polylog `π(x)` via de Branges geometry. If it fails (likely), we get a structural B-grade closure of one of the four major RH approaches as a polylog vehicle.
