    291:| §D.D43 ATTACK_VECTORS — KPZ universality / Hairer regularity structures of `D(x) := (π(x) − Li(x)) log(x) / √x` on KPZ-spaced grid `x_k = X/2 + k·⌊X^{1/3}⌋` (cross-domain: Hairer 2014 *Inventiones* regularity structures, Tracy-Widom β=2, Corwin 2012 KPZ universality survey; CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES §3 promoted PROPOSED → USED PARTIAL) | FAIL | E | First project test of any non-`√x` scaling of the PNT error term; first project Hölder regularity / wavelet-decomposition test on D(x); first project import of Hairer regularity structures / KPZ universality / Tracy-Widom β=2 limit law. **Setup**: sieve π up to X ∈ {2^18, ..., 2^24}, KPZ grid `x_k = X/2 + k·⌊X^{1/3}⌋`, n_grid 2080..32896, mpmath Li(x); plus wide-range run x ∈ [10⁴, 10⁷] (u-span 6.89, gamma resolution 0.91 — resolves first 12 ζ-zero γ_k peaks). **Pre-stated falsifiers F1–F5** registered in `d43_kpz_pi_li.py` docstring. **Result: F1 PASS (Gauss-skew on detrended Z_d, |z|<3 across all 7 logX), F2 FAIL (TW2-skew on Z_d rejected at |z|≥5 in 5/7 windows), F3 FAIL (right-tail Gauss r²=0.977 ≥ KPZ r²=0.952 at logX=22), F4 FAIL (wavelet Hölder α=0.85 stable across logX 18..24 with r²>0.998 — far above KPZ ceiling 1/2), F5 N/A.** Whole-window Z skew oscillates in [-0.187, +0.204] across logX 18..24 with NO trend toward TW2's +0.224; the apparent positive Z_raw skew at logX=22 (+0.204) and logX=24 (+0.197) is a Skewes-bias drift artifact of the asymmetric trend within [X/2, X], disappearing entirely after detrending. **Wide-range FFT** (x∈[10⁴,10⁷]) confirms D(x)'s top peaks land at the first 12 nontrivial Riemann zeta zeros γ_k, with γ_1=14.135 peak/median ratio 770000, γ_2=21.022 ratio 760000 — consistent with the explicit formula `D(x) = -log(x)·Σ_ρ x^{ρ-1}/ρ + lower order`. **Structural reason for KPZ failure**: D(x) is a deterministic almost-periodic function generated by a finite sum of zeta-zero cosines, NOT a stochastic SPDE-driven interface — KPZ class membership requires (i) stochastic white-noise input, (ii) nonlinear dynamics, (iii) macroscopic limit, NONE of which hold. The empirical wavelet α=0.85 is a smoothness signature of the sum-of-cosines structure; α=0.27 after moving-avg detrending is an artifact (residual is oscillation-dominated, fit r²<0.85). **Cramér model control** D_C with independent Bernoulli(1/log n) shows the same FFT peak pattern in same bins (random-walk artifact at sampling resolution) and similar smooth raw α≈0.95 — the chi_P / Cramér distinction lies in the deterministic-arithmetic vs stochastic origin, NOT in any KPZ-class roughness signature. **Closure mode E** (structural reduction): KPZ universality is structurally inapplicable to PNT-error-term roughness. Adds **edge E2.27** (11th orthogonal pseudorandomness category, regularity-structures / Tracy-Widom). NOT a circumvention of E3.1 / E7.18 — orthogonal scale and observable. **CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES §3** Hairer regularity structures / KPZ universality / Tracy-Widom β=2 promoted PROPOSED → USED PARTIAL with mode E and edge E2.27 reference. **Cites** E3.1 GUE pair correlation, C5 Stein method (S108), C7/E7.18 FHK (S133), S74 free cumulants, E2.13–E2.26 (13 prior orthogonal pseudorandomness categories). Cross-domain refs: Hairer 2014 *Inventiones* 198, 269 = arXiv:1303.5113; Tracy-Widom 1994 *Comm. Math. Phys.* 159, 151; Corwin 2012 = arXiv:1106.1596. See `experiments/analytic/kpz_pi_li_d43/`. | 157 |
    760:| §C1 ATTACK_VECTORS — BK arithmetic-correction probe at Odlyzko's high-height tabulated zeros (zeros4 T~1.4·10²⁰ N=10⁴, zeros5 T~1.4·10²¹ N=10⁴, L=44.6/46.8) — wild-swing extension of S49 | FAIL | I | DUPLICATE-PLUS of line 733 (S49 N=8000 closure at L=7) but with **new quantitative obstruction**. Re-ran the full BK template Pearson + per-prime Fourier amplitude + phase-coherence battery on Odlyzko's published high-height tables. Empirical Pearson(D, BK_template) = +0.063 (zeros4), +0.035 (zeros5). **Proper null** (random-prime template: replace primes with uniform pseudo-primes in [2,50] preserving template shape): null mean = +0.063 / +0.035, std = 2-4·10⁻⁴, **z-scores -0.94σ / +0.93σ** — empirical Pearson is statistically indistinguishable from random-frequency template. Direct test: prime-frequency |Fourier amplitude| median = 0.0141/0.0100 vs random-frequency 0.0148/0.0101 — **prime amplitudes NOT enhanced** (ratios 0.95, 0.99). The previously-reported gap-shuffled-null +33σ "signal" is **null-bias artefact**: gap-shuffled has Poisson-leakage in long-range tail anti-correlated with any oscillatory template, inflating apparent z-scores. **NEW QUANTITATIVE OBSTRUCTION** (sharpens E7.1, E1.10, E3.13): empirical fit `\|BK_pred\|_max · L² ≈ 13.6` (invariant across L=44.6, 46.8, confirms 1/L² scaling), `pair_rms ≈ 4/√N` (verified across N ∈ {2000, 8000, 10000}). Detection threshold: N ≥ (4κ/13.6)² · L⁴ ≈ 0.09 κ² L⁴ for κ-σ detection. **At κ=3: required N at L=44.6 is 3.5×10⁵ zeros** (Odlyzko provides 10⁴ — **35× short**); at L=46.8 is 4.2×10⁵ (**42× short**). At L=80 (T~10⁵²): N≥3·10⁷, hopeless; even at L=20 needs ~10⁵ zeros. **L⁴ scaling is structural**: doubling height L requires 16× more zeros. The asymptotic regime *suppresses* the BK signal faster than data accumulation can compensate. Cross-domain ingredient: Odlyzko's tabulated zeros at heights T ~ 10²⁰-10²¹ (numerical-analysis frontier; precision ~10⁻⁶ in γ). **First quantitative version of "BK is asymptotically too weak" obstruction in the project's catalogue.** Implies any future BK-template detection via direct R₂ residual is bounded below by N_required(L) ≥ 0.81 L⁴ — a hard scaling barrier independent of computational budget. Closes ATTACK_VECTORS §C1 with a structural negative result. Suggested EDGE upgrade: extend E7.1 from qualitative "BK undetected" to quantitative "BK detection requires N ≥ 0.81 L⁴ zeros, infeasible for any tractable L". Cites E7.1, E1.10, E3.13, S49. See experiments/analytic/zeta_structure/odlyzko_high_height/odlyzko_bk_probe_results.md. | 71 |
