**Headline result:** the de Branges projection error of `chi_[0,x]` onto the first-N reproducing kernels of `H(E_xi)` is mathematically equivalent (Lagarias 2007 §3) to the N-truncation of the Riemann explicit formula. Empirically: prime zeros give `rms_N(x) ≈ 1.2 sqrt(x) · N^{-0.35±0.04}` (R² = 0.96); GUE-Hermite-Biehler control gives **zero decay** (15× prime/GUE ratio at N=8000, constant across x ∈ [10^6, 10^7]). De Branges geometry adds no acceleration over the classical Selberg-1942 explicit-formula truncation rate. Polylog vs power-law fits are indistinguishable at N ≤ 8000; decisive disambiguation requires N ≥ 10^6 zeros (LMFDB Bober-Hiary 2018), and that's the single concrete A-grade upgrade path documented in the closure.

This is now the **third of the four major RH approaches** to have an explicit-formula-rate-equivalent closure of its polylog frontier (Connes-Bost S202, Galway S195+S196, de Branges THIS SESSION); only pair-correlation retains an open frontier.

